  "foaf:name": "Large-scale Seagrass Mapping &amp; Management Init",
  "sdo:name": "Large-scale Seagrass Mapping &amp; Management Init",
  "sdo:description": "Seagrass meadows provide food, livelihoods, and climate benefits for communities across the Western Indian Ocean (WIO). But limited data on seagrasses coverage remains a barrier to their conservation and management. The Large-Scale Seagrass Mapping and Management Initiative (LaSMMI) (www.lasmmi.org) is a research collaborative supported by The Pew Charitable Trusts, in partnership with the Western Indian Ocean Marine Science Association (WIOMSA), University of Southampton, and several research institutions and partners in the WIO region. Building on successful research completed in Seychelles, the LaSMMI project aims to create a field-verified seagrass map and estimate seagrass carbon stocks for Kenya, Tanzania, Mozambique, and Madagascar. LaSMMI also seeks to deliver the data needed to accelerate seagrass conservation and management, particularly through policies such as the Nationally Determined Contributions under the Paris Agreement.",
